## Dark Skin Nail Colours for Every Occasion

The colour that photographs beautifully at a brunch is not always the colour you want in a board meeting, and the shade that looks perfect for a Saturday is not always the one for a Saturday night. For shades that hold across all complexions and occasions, <a href='/blog/skin-tone/nail-colors-that-look-good-on-every-skin-tone'>Nail Colors That Look Good on Every Skin Tone</a> is a useful reference point  but what follows here is specific to what works on deep skin.

**Work**: the goal is polish without noise. Chocolate brown (the neutral that actually reads as neutral on dark skin), cognac, burgundy in a matte formula, and deep navy all give an intentional, finished look without reading as casual. White nails work here too  clean and crisp reads as professional, not creative-casual. Avoid bright neons and holographic chrome for formal environments unless the role calls for it.

**Date night**: this is where dark skin and nail colour get to fully commit. Deep cherry red with a high-gloss finish. Cobalt blue. A rich fuchsia. Gold chrome if the vibe is glam. Or, counterintuitively, a perfect oxblood  which has the quality of looking dramatic in candlelight while remaining genuinely elegant. Almond-shaped nails in any of these shades, on deep skin, photograph in a way that makes it immediately clear why <a href='https://mirelleinspo.com/blog/almond-nail-colors-skin-tone' target='_blank' rel='noopener'>almond nail colours for dark skin</a> have their own dedicated following.

**Weekend and everyday**: this is the space for experimenting. Saturated pastels, burnt orange, emerald, the "bold" shade you have been saving. When the stakes are lower, the colour can be higher.

